Research references:
- Kythera: Kythera's ZZZ Shader V2 (toon lighting and face shading organization).
- Jideeh: Kytheras-ZZZ-Shader v1.7.1 (head frame, eye layer and inverted hull organization).
  https://github.com/Jideeh1/Kytheras-ZZZ-Shader
- MMD Tools: public PMX import API and PMX shininess-to-roughness convention;
  installed separately by the user.
  https://github.com/MMD-Blender/blender_mmd_tools
- Hoyo-GI-Toon: PMX semantics and reversible-data workflow experience.
- VRM Consortium / MToon: separation of light-direction shading and lit/shade colors.
  https://github.com/vrm-c/vrm-specification/blob/master/specification/VRMC_materials_mtoon-1.0/README.md

Adapted GPL-3.0 source formulas:
- ImLaoBJie / RandomPlayToon, commit 87ebc01de7c6a1ab4796b7da7196b88830d74667.
  https://github.com/ImLaoBJie/RandomPlayToon
  materials/graph.py (toon and specular), detail_review.py (hair response),
  scene_response.py (regularized light chromaticity), and the sampled-region
  matching approach of source_asset_match.py. Changes are integrated in
  materials/surface.py and surface_inputs.py, with PMX ownership, region gating,
  source preservation and lifecycle handling implemented here. Version 0.5 also
  studies vivian_parity.py (shared display light/shadow separation), light_color.py
  (bounded colour response) and surface_refinement.py (view/key-dependent broad
  reflection). Its three-band palette, saturation-gated ambient colour, skin
  palette and common cloth response are implemented in materials/surface.py.
  Character presets, per-character material patches and authored face fields
  are not included. The upstream GPL license is compatible with this GPLv3 work.

This candidate contains native-node builders and its own workflow code.
Research .blend files, character models, game textures and private verification assets
are not included. BASIC remains a generic face approximation; SDF mode uses a
separately selected, UV-matched shared Lightmap. The SDF direction curve, mirrored
sampling and R/Alpha mask math were studied from the local Kythera V2 reference.
Its native-light receiver and reversible PMX integration are implemented here.
The frozen 0.3 palette studied the native Lit/Shadow HSV curves. Versions 0.4/0.5
use the shared surface implementations described above; they are not a port of
the complete game renderer or of character-specific RandomPlayToon presets.
